keyhole watches a LAN for the resets and block pages Korean ISPs use to
censor sites, confirms each suspected domain with active probes, and
bypasses censorship for the confirmed domains only. It also serves as the
DNS forwarder behind Unbound, relaying queries to the configured upstream.

The plugin provides the settings page, service control and firewall
anchors; the keyhole daemon itself is installed at /usr/local/sbin/keyhole.
